+# Contract: `POST /v1/executions/{id}/signal` — reply envelope & recognized-retry proof
+
+**Feature**: 001-bench · **Phase 1 output**
+
+This contract documents the caller-facing reply shapes of the signal endpoint of the Runtime API (`graphhelm serve`), focused on what changes in this feature: the recognized-retry proof gains `signalId` for signal retries only. It is the observable wire contract — no checked-in documentation file previously pinned this shape (spec assumption: "the observable contract is defined by the code and by the tests that freeze it"), so this document plus the HTTP tests are the reference from now on.
+
+## Endpoint
+
+- **Method / path**: `POST /v1/executions/{id}/signal`
+- **Auth**: bearer token issued by the server (same as every Runtime API route).
+- **Headers**:
+  - `Idempotency-Key: <key>` — required for mutations; stable per logical submission.
+  - `X-GraphHelm-Actor: <actor-id>` + `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Type: <type>` — durable actor attribution.
+  - `If-Match: <headSequence>` — optional, fresh mutations only (advisory fast-fail; stale on recognized retries is moot).
+- **Body**: `{ "signal": {…envelope…}, "evidenceOut": "<path>"? }` — envelope validated by the signal schema; `evidenceOut` required unless the server runs with a keyring.
+
+All replies below use the standard envelope `{ "ok": bool, "command": "execution.signal", "data": {…}, "diagnostics": [ … ] }`.
+
+## Reply class 1 — Fresh submission (UNCHANGED)
+
+`200 OK`, bespoke data built by the signal command:
+
+```json
+{
+  "ok": true,
+  "command": "execution.signal",
+  "data": {
+    "executionId": "exec-…",
+    "signalId": "signal-http-retry",
+    "kind": "no_progress",
+    "mayProposeMutation": false,
+    "decision": "requires_approval",
+    "rejectionReason": null,
+    "headSequence": 4
+  },
+  "diagnostics": []
+}
+```
+
+`data.signalId` is the durable identifier of the committed decision. **No `idempotency` object on fresh submissions.**
+
+## Reply class 2 — Recognized retry (CHANGED for signals)
+
+`200 OK`, current execution status (the same read `GET /v1/executions/{id}` serves) plus the additive proof:
+
+```json
+{
+  "ok": true,
+  "command": "execution.signal",
+  "data": {
+    "…current status snapshot…": "…",
+    "headSequence": 7,
+    "idempotency": {
+      "recognizedRetry": true,
+      "originalDecisionSequence": 3,
+      "signalId": "signal-http-retry"
+    }
+  },
+  "diagnostics": []
+}
+```
+
+### `data.idempotency` — recognized-retry proof (all mutation commands)
+
+| Field | Type | Command scope | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `recognizedRetry` | `true` | every mutation command | pre-existing |
+| `originalDecisionSequence` | `integer` | every mutation command | pre-existing — sequence of the first committed decision event |
+| `signalId` | `string` | **`execution.signal` only** | **NEW** — `signal_recorded.signal_id` of the authenticated committed decision; byte-identical to the first reply's `data.signalId`; stable across any number of retries and unaffected by later state advancement |
+
+The proof appears **only** on recognized retries (classification `Complete`: same derived key ⇒ same key header + identical body digest + same actor + matching decision kind + matching execution/scope/stream). It never appears on: plain reads, fresh submissions, or any refusal.
+
+### Invariants
+
+1. On a signal retry, `retry.data.idempotency.signalId == first.data.signalId == committed event's signalId`.
+2. Repeating the retry any number of times, at later heads, always returns the same `signalId`.
+3. Every other mutation command's proof remains exactly `{recognizedRetry, originalDecisionSequence}` — no new field anywhere else.
+4. The retry still reports **current** status (`headSequence` may be newer than `originalDecisionSequence`) and appends nothing to the store.
+
+## Reply class 3 — Fail-closed refusals (UNCHANGED)
+
+`409 Conflict` with `ok: false` and diagnostic code `GHE003_IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT` when:
+- the same key+body arrives from a **different authenticated actor**,
+- the key already resolves to a committed event of a **different decision kind** (or divergent body reuse under the same key),
+- a previous attempt applied only partially.
+
+```json
+{
+  "ok": false,
+  "command": "execution.signal",
+  "data": { "currentHead": 3 },
+  "diagnostics": [
+    { "code": "GHE003_IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT", "severity": "error", "path": "/idempotencyKey", "message": "…" }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Refusals carry **no** `idempotency` object and **no** `signalId`; they disclose nothing new about the original decision (not its actor, kind, or identity) and append nothing.
+
+## Scope note
+
+Only the signal endpoint's recognized-retry reply shape changes. `execution.start`, `approve`, `amend_budget`, `pause`, `resume`, `cancel`, `sweep`, `wake_lease`, `claim`, `clear` keep their exact current proof surface. Recognition rules, refusal paths, CLI face, and wire identifiers are untouched.
