+# Data Model: Signal Identity on Recognized Retries (001-bench)
+
+**Date**: 2026-10-26 · **Phase 1 output**
+
+Entities are extracted from the feature spec's *Key Entities* and grounded in the checked-in code of this checkout. No persistence changes in this feature: one entity is an existing durable record, the other is a per-reply annotation that gains a field.
+
+## Entity 1 — Signal decision record (durable)
+
+**Where it lives**: append-only Event Store stream for one execution; wire event kind `signal_recorded`; typed as `SignalRecorded` (`core/protocols/src/event.rs:965-973`, `#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase", deny_unknown_fields)]`).
+
+| Field (wire / type) | Type | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `executionId` / `execution_id` | `OpaqueId` | Owning execution; must equal the request's execution for recognition. |
+| `signalId` / `signal_id` | `OpaqueId` | **The original durable signal identifier.** Created once at admission; the value the first reply returned as `data.signalId`. Never rewritten. |
+| `sourceType` / `source_kind` | `SignalSourceKind` | Source kind (e.g., `node`); verified against the retried envelope. |
+| `sourceId` / `source_id` | `OpaqueId` | Source identity; verified against the retried envelope. |
+| `kind` / `kind` | `String` | Raw signal type string (preserved even if unrecognized). |
+| `severity` / `severity` | `SignalSeverity` | Enum; verified against the retried envelope. |
+| `envelopeSha256` / `envelope_sha256` | `RawSha256` | Digest of the canonicalized envelope bytes — binds the record to the exact admitted evidence. Recognition re-digests the retried `signal` object and requires equality. |
+| Envelope (event level) | — | `actor`, `scope`, `streamId`, `sequence`, `idempotencyKey` — all part of the recognition identity, all pre-existing. |
+
+**Validation rules** (pre-existing, untouched by this feature):
+- Envelope must validate schema-wise before admission (`admit_signal` → `InvalidSignal` refused).
+- `signalId`/`sourceId` must be wire-representable (`UnrecordableIdentity` otherwise refuses with evidence preserved).
+- Free-form content never stored inline (D-036): description/envelope externalized as Evidence; only `envelopeSha256` binds them.
+- Keying: the appended event carries the server-derived idempotency key `{Idempotency-Key}-record-{digest16}`; a byte-identical retry re-derives the identical key.
+
+**Lifecycle**: created exactly once per committed decision by the first successful `POST /v1/executions/{id}/signal`; immutable forever; read on every recognized retry via the classifier's history scan. No state transitions of the record itself.
+
+## Entity 2 — Recognized-retry proof (per-reply annotation)
+
+**Where it lives**: only inside HTTP `200` replies served by `reply_with_current_status` when key classification returns `Complete`. Not persisted, not part of any event or projection — rebuilt on every reply from the store read.
+
+| Field | Type | Present when |
+|---|---|---|
+| `recognizedRetry` | `bool` (always `true`) | every recognized retry reply (all mutation commands) — pre-existing |
+| `originalDecisionSequence` | `u64` | every recognized retry reply — sequence of the first committed decision event for the command — pre-existing |
+| `signalId` | `string` (`OpaqueId` spelling) | **NEW — only when the command is `execution.signal`**; value = `SignalRecorded.signal_id` of the authenticated committed event (Entity 1). Never present for other commands, fresh submissions, plain reads, or refusals. |
+
+**Placement**: inside `data.idempotency` of the JSON reply envelope — the one annotation scoped to "this reply proves a retry of that decision", keeping the shared status-snapshot shape (plain reads, other commands) free of the new field.
+
+**Validation rules introduced by this feature**:
+1. `signalId` appears **iff** the key classified as `Complete` for `execution.signal` — recognition already required identical body, same actor, same scope/stream/execution, matching `signal_recorded` kind, and `sha256(signal) == envelopeSha256`; the identifier is taken from that authenticated record, so no new failure mode exists (spec assumption adopted).
+2. Byte-identity with the first reply's `data.signalId` (SC-001) — holds because both read the same immutable field.
+3. Stability across repeats (acceptance scenario 3) — holds because the store is append-only and the scan always finds the same decision event.
+4. Refusal paths fail closed (FR-004/FR-005): `Divergent` (mismatched actor or divergent reuse) and `Partial` replies carry **no** `idempotency` object at all; nothing newly disclosed (no actor, no kind, no id).
+5. Other mutation commands keep exactly `{recognizedRetry, originalDecisionSequence}` — structurally guaranteed because only `SignalRecorded` yields the identifier (R4 in research).
+
+**Relationships**:
+```
+recognized retry reply ──(originalDecisionSequence)──▶ signal_recorded event (Entity 1)
+                                                        │ .signalId
+reply.data.idempotency.signalId ◀───────────────────────┘
+first reply.data.signalId          ◀────────────────────────┘   (same value, by construction)
+```
+
+## State transitions (reply classes, per command outcome)
+
+Pre-existing transitions unchanged; the only delta is the proof content on the `Complete` arm for signals:
+
+| Request outcome | Reply | `idempotency` block (pre → post change, signal command) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Fresh submission | 200, bespoke `data` incl. `signalId`, no proof | absent → absent |
+| Recognized retry (Complete), signal | 200, current status + proof | `{recognizedRetry, originalDecisionSequence}` → `{recognizedRetry, originalDecisionSequence, signalId}` |
+| Recognized retry (Complete), other command | 200, current status + proof | `{recognizedRetry, originalDecisionSequence}` (unchanged) |
+| Divergent (different actor / different body under same header) | 409 `GHE003_IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT` | absent (unchanged) |
+| Wrong-kind committed event under the key | 409 `GHE003_IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT` | absent (unchanged) |
+| Partial (stuck half-applied attempt) | 409, names first missing key | absent (unchanged) |
+| Plain `GET` status | 200, status snapshot | absent (unchanged) |
