+# Implementation Plan: Signal Identity on Recognized Retries
+
+**Branch**: `main` (Stage Setup `BRANCH`; spec feature-branch label `001-bench`) | **Date**: 2026-10-26 | **Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)
+
+**Input**: Feature specification from `/specs/001-bench/spec.md`
+
+## Summary
+
+The Runtime API endpoint `POST /v1/executions/{id}/signal` already answers a recognized idempotent retry (same `Idempotency-Key`, identical body, same authenticated actor, matching decision kind) with HTTP 200, the current execution status, and an additive `data.idempotency` retry proof carrying `recognizedRetry: true` plus `originalDecisionSequence`. That proof does **not** carry the original durable `signalId` that the first (fresh) reply returned in `data.signalId`, so a client retrying after a lost acknowledgement cannot match its sent signal against the committed record.
+
+Technical approach (from research): the serve layer's key classifier already loads the full stream history once and verifies the committed `signal_recorded` event field-by-field against the request envelope, including `payload.signal_id == request.signal.id` and the `envelope_sha256` digest. The identifier is therefore available **in the same single history scan** that classifies the key. The change threads one optional value (`Option<String>`) from `classify_one_key` through `KeyPresence::Present` / `KeyState::Complete` into `reply_with_current_status` → `reply_with_status_value` → `annotate_recognized_retry`, which inserts `signalId` into the existing proof object when present. No new endpoint, no new event, no change to recognition rules, refusal paths, or any other command. Proof: a new regression assertion in `apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs` that fails pre-change (SC-004) and the two existing exact-shape signal-retry proof tests updated to the enriched shape (per spec Edge Cases).
+
+## Technical Context
+
+**Language/Version**: Rust `1.97.1` (pinned toolchain, `AGENTS.md`; `rustfmt` + `clippy` components)
+
+**Primary Dependencies**: all pre-existing workspace crates and crates.io deps — `serde_json`, `axum`, `tokio`, `tempfile`, `assert_cmd`, `graphhelm-protocols`, `graphhelm-events`, `graphhelm-policy`, `graphhelm-simulation`. **No new dependency** (Keel: a new dependency would have to be named in the PR body; there is none).
+
+**Storage**: local append-only event store (`graphhelm_events::LocalEventRepository`, file-based committed batches under the `--events` directory). This change only READS the stream history (via `execution::resolve_stream`) — no new persistence, no schema change.
+
+**Testing**: `cargo test` — integration tests in `apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs` (live-server HTTP journey against a spawned `graphhelm serve`) plus private unit tests inside `apps/cli/src/commands/serve/mod.rs` (two-writer race cell, non-object-status 500 cell). Tests are offline, use fixed IDs/clocks per repo policy.
+
+**Target Platform**: Windows PowerShell dev machine (all commands must work there); code is platform-neutral core/CLI Rust that must also compile/test on Linux.
+
+**Project Type**: CLI + embedded Runtime HTTP API in a Rust workspace (`apps/cli` bin crate; business rules kept out of the bin where possible, but the idempotency layer legitimately lives in the serve command module).
+
+**Performance Goals**: no numeric goal — the identifier rides the history scan `classify_existing_keys` already performs (one store open, one `resolve_stream`). No second scan, no second store open, no network.
+
+**Constraints**:
+- Offline tests: no internet, Docker, credentials, provider accounts, browser sessions, or production infrastructure.
+- Fail-closed refusals: divergent actor / wrong decision kind keep today's 409 `GHE003_IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT` shape — **no** `idempotency` object, **no** `signalId`, nothing newly disclosed.
+- The identifier comes from the committed decision record, never from current state or caller-supplied values.
+- Structured errors only; no new diagnostics needed unless annotation itself fails (existing `IDEMPOTENCY_REPLY_CODE` path unchanged).
+- Recognition rules untouched: same key + identical body + same actor + matching decision kind, exactly as today.
+- Pinned toolchain, `--locked` everywhere; no new public modules/types/functions beyond private signature widening inside `serve/mod.rs`.
+
+**Scale/Scope**: 1 source file changed (`apps/cli/src/commands/serve/mod.rs`), 2 test files touched (`apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs`; the private test module in `serve/mod.rs`). One additive JSON field on one reply class. Everything else byte-identical.
