+## Phase 4: User Story 2 - A mismatched actor still receives no retry proof and no signal identity (Priority: P2)
+
+**Goal**: When the same `Idempotency-Key` + identical body arrives from a **different authenticated actor**, the reply is exactly today's fail-closed 409 `GHE003_IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT` — no `idempotency` object, no `signalId`, no newly disclosed information about the original decision (not its actor, kind, or identity), and nothing appended. The new identifier must not open a disclosure channel on this refusal path.
+
+**Independent Test**: Commit a signal under a key as agent A; resend the same key + body as agent B; verify the refusal is unchanged — no retry proof, no signal identifier, nothing appended.
+
+> No source change is required for this story: the `Divergent` refusal path (`divergent_conflict_response`, ~line 1875) never reaches `annotate_recognized_retry`, so it is structurally impossible for it to gain the field. This story is the guardrail that PROVES the plumbing in T007 did not leak onto the refusal path.
