+## Dependencies & Execution Order
+
+### Phase Dependencies
+
+- **Setup (Phase 1)**: No dependencies — start immediately.
+- **Foundational (Phase 2)**: Depends on Setup. BLOCKS all user stories (confirms the edit sites and helpers every story uses).
+- **User Stories (Phases 3–5)**: All depend on Foundational. Within US1, the RED test (T006) precedes the implementation (T007) which precedes GREEN (T008) and the exact-shape updates (T009, T010). US2 (T011) and US3 (T012) depend on the US1 engine (T007) existing so their no-leak property is observable, but depend on NO other story's logic.
+- **Polish (Phase 6)**: Depends on US1 (and, for full coverage, US2/US3) being complete.
+
+### User Story Dependencies
+
+- **US1 (P1)**: After Foundational. The single self-contained increment. No dependency on US2/US3.
+- **US2 (P2)**: After the US1 engine exists (T007). Independently testable; needs no source change of its own.
+- **US3 (P3)**: After the US1 engine exists (T007). Independently testable; needs no source change of its own.
+
+### Within Each User Story
+
+- Tests are written and observed to FAIL (RED) before implementation (US1: T006 before T007).
+- Engine before the exact-shape updates it forces (T007 → T009/T010).
+- Refusal-path guardrails verified only after the mechanism that could leak onto them exists.
+- Story complete before moving to the next priority.
+
+### Parallel Opportunities
+
+- **Phase 1**: T002 [P] is logically independent of T001's bookkeeping (though both read the same tree; run sequentially if sharing one target dir to avoid a package-cache lock stall).
+- **Within US1**: T009 [US1] (edits `apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs`) and T010 [US1] (edits `apps/cli/src/commands/serve/mod.rs`) touch **different files** and could be dispatched together after T007 — but both re-run overlapping test targets, so schedule them sequentially if sharing a target dir to avoid cargo lock contention.
+- **US2 / US3**: T011 [US2] and T012 [US3] both run filtered cells in `apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs`; they are logically independent guardrails and may be worked in parallel by two readers (different assertions, read-mostly edits).
+- **Phase 6**: T013, T014, T015, T016 [P] are distinct observation surfaces (HTTP integration vs lib unit vs style vs end-to-end evidence) and can be dispatched together, subject to the shared cargo target/package-cache lock — coordinate so concurrent `cargo` invocations queue on the lock rather than relaunch.
