+## Implementation Strategy
+
+### MVP First (User Story 1 Only)
+
+1. Complete Phase 1: Setup (toolchain + pre-change green baseline).
+2. Complete Phase 2: Foundational (confirm edit sites + helpers).
+3. Complete Phase 3: User Story 1 (RED test T006 → engine T007 → GREEN T008 → exact-shape updates T009/T010).
+4. **STOP and VALIDATE**: run the US1 regression test (GREEN) plus the pre-change baseline cells (T002 set) to show no regression.
+5. US1 alone delivers the entire user-visible value: a lost-acknowledgement signal retry is lossless for signal identity.
+
+### Incremental Delivery
+
+1. Setup + Foundational → edit sites and helpers confirmed.
+2. Add US1 → validate independently → **MVP** (SC-001/SC-004).
+3. Add US2 → validate independently → the mismatched-actor refusal leaks nothing (SC-002).
+4. Add US3 → validate independently → the wrong-kind refusal leaks nothing (SC-002).
+5. Polish (Phase 6) → full minimal validation surface green; hand off to delivery.
+
+### Notes on the guardrail stories (US2/US3)
+
+These stories require **no new code**; their value is proof that the US1 engine (T007) did not widen the disclosure surface of the fail-closed refusal paths. Each is a focused run-and-confirm (with optional strengthening of the existing cell's assertions to explicitly pin "no `signalId`"). If strengthened, the strengthened cell still observes a real boundary (a refusal must not disclose the identifier) and is not coverage relaxation.
